1
00:00:08,031 --> 00:00:11,971
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:12,724 --> 00:00:15,765
إن الحمد لله، نحمده ونستعينه ونستغفره ونستهديه،

3
00:00:15,879 --> 00:00:18,859
ونعوذ بالله من شرور أنفسنا ومن سيئات أعمالنا،

4
00:00:19,319 --> 00:00:22,152
من يهده الله فلا مضل له ومن يضلل فلا هادي له،

5
00:00:22,345 --> 00:00:26,745
وأشهد أن لا إله إلا الله وأشهد أن محمدرسول الله، امَّا بعد

6
00:00:28,225 --> 00:00:31,325
 ونحمدالله عزوجل الذى بنعمت اجتمع الصالحات

7
00:00:31,852 --> 00:00:39,538
We praise Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, whom without Him, no good could happened and all blessings are from Him.

8
00:00:40,205 --> 00:00:44,907
We thank Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and we say; Alhamdulillah(اَلْحَمْدُ لله) and then; Alhamdulillah(اَلْحَمْدُ لله) and then; Alhamdulillah(اَلْحَمْدُ لله);

9
00:00:45,481 --> 00:00:47,399
Who made it possible for us to worship Him.

10
00:00:47,793 --> 00:00:51,756
If it wasn't for Him allowing us and assisting us to do so;

11
00:00:52,263 --> 00:01:01,105
we wouldn't have been able to make one Tasbeeha(تسبيهه) or one Tahlila(تحليله) or one Takbeera(تكبيره) or one Raka'ah(ركعه) or to fast one day.

12
00:01:02,025 --> 00:01:05,609
It is all from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and his Tawfeeq(توفيق) and assistance.

13
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:19,853
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى saved Musa(موسى) and Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) from the strongest man and regime and army and nation, on the face of the earth.

14
00:01:21,859 --> 00:01:24,829
To Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; there is nothing that is the superpower.

15
00:01:25,895 --> 00:01:27,802
There is no one who is strong.

16
00:01:28,469 --> 00:01:30,294
There is no government that is powerful.

17
00:01:31,474 --> 00:01:35,321
For Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; they are all under Him and they are all His servants.

18
00:01:37,154 --> 00:01:45,334
And for Allahسُبحانه وتعالى with Kun Fayakun(كُن فَيَكُون); everything is created or anything can be destroyed.

19
00:01:47,448 --> 00:01:49,596
وَإِذْ أَنجَيْنَاكُم مِّنْ آلِ فِرْعَوْنَ

20
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:56,188
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; We saved you from Firaun(فرعون) and his people.

21
00:01:57,222 --> 00:01:59,165
Blessing from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

22
00:01:59,615 --> 00:02:04,031
Banu Israel(بنو اسرائيل) saw the miracle of Allah in front of their own eyes.

23
00:02:04,844 --> 00:02:11,413
They saw the sea split into two portions which seemed like mountains.

24
00:02:12,053 --> 00:02:15,376
And then they saw Firaun(فرعون) and his army drowning.

25
00:02:16,196 --> 00:02:19,709
And they saw how Allahسُبحانه وتعالى delivered them to safety.

26
00:02:20,743 --> 00:02:24,182
What was the first thing they did, when they reached to safety?

27
00:02:25,155 --> 00:02:30,105
Banu Israel(بنو اسرائيل) the first thing they did, when they were with Musa(موسى),

28
00:02:30,725 --> 00:02:38,621
 when they were traveling into a new land, finally they are in freedom now, released from the servitude of Firaun(فرعون)?

29
00:02:38,934 --> 00:02:46,593
Banu Israel(بنو اسرائيل) saw some men worshipping some idols.

30
00:02:48,093 --> 00:02:51,056
They went to Musa(موسى) and they said;

31
00:02:51,076 --> 00:02:54,142
ٱجْعَل لَّنَآ إِلَٰهًا كَمَا لَهُمْ ءَالِهَةٌ ۚ

32
00:02:54,829 --> 00:03:00,855
They said; Oh Musa(موسى)! Can you create for us or make for us a god, like they have gods.

33
00:03:02,728 --> 00:03:04,037
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

34
00:03:04,124 --> 00:03:20,058
وَجَٰوَزْنَا بِبَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ ٱلْبَحْرَ فَأَتَوْاْ عَلَىٰ قَوْمٍۢ يَعْكُفُونَ عَلَىٰٓ أَصْنَامٍۢ لَّهُمْ ۚ

35
00:03:20,545 --> 00:03:29,464
قَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَى ٱجْعَل لَّنَآ إِلَٰهًا كَمَا لَهُمْ ءَالِهَةٌ ۚ

36
00:03:29,761 --> 00:03:33,405
And we brought the children of Israel(اسرائيل) with safety across the sea,

37
00:03:33,571 --> 00:03:37,851
and they came upon people devoted to some of their idols in worship.

38
00:03:38,171 --> 00:03:43,265
They said; Oh Moses! Make for us a God as they have Gods.

39
00:03:44,199 --> 00:03:47,789
Subhanallahil-Azeem(سُبحَانَ اللهِ العَظِيم)! you just came out from Egypt.

40
00:03:48,195 --> 00:03:54,684
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى saved you and you saw the miracles of Allah with your own eyes.

41
00:03:55,191 --> 00:04:03,290
You saw the miracles of Allah, assisting Musa(موسى) and assisting you and you were helpless and you couldn't do anything for yourselves.

42
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:07,469
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى performs these miracles in front of your own eyes.

43
00:04:07,749 --> 00:04:12,122
And then you ask Musa(موسى) to create for you a god, like they have Gods.

44
00:04:13,022 --> 00:04:18,099
Banu Israel(بنو اسرائيل) they knew about Allah and they believed in Allah, Don't understand this wrong.

45
00:04:18,452 --> 00:04:21,741
Don't think that Banu Israel(بنو اسرائيل) wanted to replace the religion with something else.

46
00:04:21,781 --> 00:04:22,607
 No!

47
00:04:22,834 --> 00:04:28,296
They believed in Allah and they knew that Allah is the one who helped them and assisted them.

48
00:04:28,876 --> 00:04:34,973
But when they saw what the other people are doing, they wanted to have something similar to them.

49
00:04:34,993 --> 00:04:37,026
They are not satisfied with what they had.

50
00:04:37,066 --> 00:04:38,886
They have an inferiority complex.

51
00:04:40,319 --> 00:04:45,401
So they think that these gods are gonna bring them closer to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى or something.

52
00:04:46,288 --> 00:04:47,911
Ibn Khaldoon(اِبن خَلدُون) says something interesting.

53
00:04:47,931 --> 00:04:53,303
He says that, always weak nations imitate the strong nations.

54
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:55,903
الضعيف يتشبه بالقوي

55
00:04:56,903 --> 00:04:59,469
The weak imitates the strong.

56
00:05:00,029 --> 00:05:04,500
Banu Israel(بنو اسرائيل) were weak in Egypt, and they came out of Egypt,

57
00:05:04,686 --> 00:05:08,882
now they are in freedom, but they're still thinking with the weak mentality.

58
00:05:10,795 --> 00:05:14,422
So they always think that the others have something better than them.

59
00:05:15,291 --> 00:05:18,264
And you find among the Muslims who are weak today,

60
00:05:18,917 --> 00:05:22,566
those of them who are not proud with what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given them,

61
00:05:22,753 --> 00:05:26,353
they're always trying to find ways to imitate the others.

62
00:05:27,181 --> 00:05:28,430
And who are they imitating?

63
00:05:28,455 --> 00:05:30,115
They're imitating the West.

64
00:05:30,329 --> 00:05:31,715
Because the West is strong.

65
00:05:32,235 --> 00:05:35,771
So you find that the Muslim wants to look like the non-believers.

66
00:05:36,091 --> 00:05:38,764
He wants to act like the non-believers.

67
00:05:38,984 --> 00:05:41,411
He wants to celebrate like the non-believers.

68
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:45,450
He wants to do everything; the way the non-believers are acting.

69
00:05:47,024 --> 00:05:53,449
One of the prominent priests of the Catholic Church in Italy.

70
00:05:54,249 --> 00:05:57,125
So this priest wrote a letter to the Pope.

71
00:05:57,778 --> 00:06:04,240
In that letter, he said; If you would just see the state of our Christian men;

72
00:06:04,307 --> 00:06:07,520
he was talking about Alfursaan(اَلفُرسَان); these are the Knights.

73
00:06:08,294 --> 00:06:11,505
The Christian churches to send these Knights to raid the Muslim world,

74
00:06:11,552 --> 00:06:17,391
they would go to the Holy Land and these were very powerful small bands of horsemen.

75
00:06:17,551 --> 00:06:21,313
And then they would dispatch them to the Muslim world to cause corruption.

76
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:26,107
And by the way, not only were they causing corruption on land, but it also happened in the sea.

77
00:06:26,333 --> 00:06:27,793
Do you know who the pirates?

78
00:06:28,226 --> 00:06:29,346
What are the pirates?

79
00:06:29,553 --> 00:06:30,833
How were the pirates founded?

80
00:06:30,993 --> 00:06:32,373
And do you know, who they were fighting?

81
00:06:33,186 --> 00:06:38,855
Piracy; the whole issue of piracy and pirates in the sea, which we see a lot of cartoons and movies about.

82
00:06:39,029 --> 00:06:43,491
It was started and invented to fight the Muslims in the Mediterranean Sea.

83
00:06:44,344 --> 00:06:45,877
That is how piracy started.

84
00:06:46,077 --> 00:06:50,387
Because the Mediterranean Sea was an Islamic sea for a very long time,

85
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:55,759
with Al-Abbaseen(اَلعَبَّاسِين) and then Al-Usmaneen(اَلعُثمَانِين) was the power in the Mediterranean Sea.

86
00:06:55,966 --> 00:07:03,042
So these pirates would go and they would raid the Muslim merchant; who are travelling in the Mediterranean Sea, anyway.

87
00:07:03,327 --> 00:07:06,217
So this priest wrote a letter to the Pope.

88
00:07:06,237 --> 00:07:14,526
He said; If you would see how our men try to dress like the Muslims and they learn Arabic

89
00:07:15,213 --> 00:07:19,745
and they write poetry of romance and love in Arabic better, than the Arabs.

90
00:07:20,712 --> 00:07:22,558
Because the Muslims in that time were strong.

91
00:07:22,578 --> 00:07:24,758
So you find that the weak is always trying to imitate the strong.

92
00:07:24,778 --> 00:07:26,215
And now, things reversed.

93
00:07:26,482 --> 00:07:30,854
So you have know, the Muslim is trying to imitate the ones who are strong.

94
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,887
But the Muslim should always believe that the strength is from Allah.

95
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,781
And the honor belongs to Allah.

96
00:07:36,821 --> 00:07:40,141
العِزَّةُ للَّهِ‏ِ ولِرَسولِهِ ولِلمُؤمِنينَ‏

97
00:07:40,187 --> 00:07:45,854
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; All honor belongs to Allah and His messenger and to the believers.

98
00:07:46,134 --> 00:07:50,256
What we are going through now is a temporary state; it is not permanent.

99
00:07:50,936 --> 00:07:56,156
So Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) are still thinking with that inferior; weak mentality.

100
00:07:56,649 --> 00:07:57,009
So, they said;

101
00:07:57,034 --> 00:08:00,474
ٱجْعَل لَّنَآ ءَالِهَةٌ ۚ ٱجْعَل لَّنَآ إِلَٰهًا كَمَا لَهُمْ ءَالِهَةٌ ۚ

102
00:08:00,691 --> 00:08:04,568
This action in itself; is it a sin or is it Kuffr(كفر)?

103
00:08:05,621 --> 00:08:06,634
It is Kuffr(كفر).

104
00:08:07,214 --> 00:08:08,638
It is disbelief.

105
00:08:09,241 --> 00:08:12,270
When you're asking for a god, besides Allah that is Kuffr(كفر).

106
00:08:12,816 --> 00:08:14,313
But what did Musa(موسى) tell them?

107
00:08:14,783 --> 00:08:17,363
Did he say you are non believers, you are Kuffar(كفار)?

108
00:08:18,132 --> 00:08:18,785
No, he didn't.

109
00:08:18,885 --> 00:08:19,372
He said;

110
00:08:19,545 --> 00:08:22,054
أَنتُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُونَ۝

111
00:08:22,208 --> 00:08:23,908
You are people who are ignorant.

112
00:08:25,408 --> 00:08:27,320
So he excuse them with their ignorance,

113
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:32,794
but he taught them, and whoever refuses after they received the message, then that is disbelief.

114
00:08:33,394 --> 00:08:35,300
So Musa(موسى) now is teaching them; he said;

115
00:08:35,354 --> 00:08:37,750
قَالَ إِنَّكُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُونَ۝

116
00:08:37,910 --> 00:08:39,810
You are people who are ignorant.

117
00:08:40,016 --> 00:08:41,063
And then he told them;

118
00:08:41,296 --> 00:08:57,535
إِنَّ هَؤُلَاءِ مُتَبَّرٌ مَا هُمْ فِيهِ وَبَاطِلٌ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ۝

119
00:08:57,733 --> 00:09:04,518
Verily, these people will be destroyed; for that which they engaged in, and all that they're doing is in vain.

120
00:09:04,738 --> 00:09:09,231
These people don't think that they're strong; don't think that they're powerful; they are going to be destroyed,

121
00:09:09,251 --> 00:09:10,378
what they're doing is; wrong.

122
00:09:10,678 --> 00:09:20,954
قَالَ أَغَيْرَ اللَّهِ أَبْغِيكُمْ إِلَٰهًا وَهُوَ فَضَّلَكُمْ عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ۝

123
00:09:21,344 --> 00:09:28,067
He said; Shall I seek for you a god other than Allah while, He Has given you superiority over mankind?

124
00:09:28,347 --> 00:09:31,387
Musa(موسى) is telling Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) that, Allah has chosen you.

125
00:09:31,767 --> 00:09:33,661
They were the chosen people of Allah.

126
00:09:33,947 --> 00:09:35,712
They were the nation whom Allah chose.

127
00:09:36,005 --> 00:09:42,502
Even though up to that moment, they were still weak, and they didn't have any Khilafah(خِلَافَه), and they didn't have any nation, and they didn't have any power.

128
00:09:42,715 --> 00:09:44,592
Nevertheless, they were still the best.

129
00:09:45,892 --> 00:09:49,791
And the Muslims need to read the Ayah(آية) of Qur'an, where Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

130
00:09:49,831 --> 00:09:51,891
كُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ

131
00:09:52,031 --> 00:09:54,551
You were the best nation produced for mankind.

132
00:09:54,811 --> 00:09:57,823
You are the best nation that was brought forth for humanity.

133
00:09:58,383 --> 00:10:00,876
So even if we are in a slump in a weak moment,

134
00:10:01,109 --> 00:10:08,949
we should still understand and realize that we have; what can make us the best and the chosen people of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

135
00:10:09,189 --> 00:10:14,543
So Musa(موسى) is telling Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) that; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you superiority over mankind.

136
00:10:14,703 --> 00:10:15,750
 He has chosen you.

137
00:10:16,663 --> 00:10:25,655
Musa(موسى) and Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) left Egypt, and they were promised the Holy Land, Jerusalem and the land surrounding it.

138
00:10:26,809 --> 00:10:29,577
So Musa(موسى) and Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) are traveled toward that direction.

139
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:33,024
They arrived next to Jerusalem.

140
00:10:33,391 --> 00:10:36,212
Musa(موسى) told his people; Let's attack!

141
00:10:36,919 --> 00:10:40,539
Here's Jerusalem, we can see it with our own eyes; Let's attack!

142
00:10:41,239 --> 00:10:47,488
In that time, it was ruled by Al-Amaleeq(اَلْعَمَالِيْق); certain disbelieving nation.

143
00:10:47,934 --> 00:10:50,057
They were the rulers of the Holy Land.

144
00:10:50,343 --> 00:10:55,290
And Musa(موسى) told Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); Allah has promised you with this land; so let's attack!

145
00:10:56,303 --> 00:11:14,467
وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِۦ يَٰقَوْمِ ٱذْكُرُواْ نِعْمَةَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذْ جَعَلَ فِيكُمْ أَنۢبِيَآءَ وَجَعَلَكُم مُّلُوكًا وَءَاتَىٰكُم

146
00:11:15,087 --> 00:11:23,925
وَءَاتَىٰكُم مَّا لَمْ يُؤْتِ أَحَدًا مِّنَ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ۝

147
00:11:24,425 --> 00:11:37,138
يَا قَوْمِ ادْخُلُوا الْأَرْضَ الْمُقَدَّسَةَ الَّتِي كَتَبَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ وَلَا تَرْتَدُّوا عَلَىٰ أَدْبَارِكُمْ

148
00:11:37,591 --> 00:11:48,861
 وَلَا تَرْتَدُّوا عَلَىٰ أَدْبَارِكُمْ فَتَنقَلِبُوا خَاسِرِينَ۝

149
00:11:49,334 --> 00:11:54,584
Oh my people! enter the Holy Land which Allah has assigned to you.

150
00:11:55,297 --> 00:11:57,457
Do not turn back in fighting.

151
00:11:58,131 --> 00:11:59,580
الفرار من الزحف

152
00:12:00,067 --> 00:12:04,040
Turning your back in the battle; is one of the major sins in Islam.

153
00:12:05,254 --> 00:12:08,547
Rasool Allah ﷺ has counted in one Hadith(حديث); seven major sins.

154
00:12:08,607 --> 00:12:09,587
One of them is;

155
00:12:09,893 --> 00:12:11,213
الفرار من الزحف

156
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:14,142
Turning your back to the battlefield and running away.

157
00:12:14,375 --> 00:12:19,409
It's a major sin and the Ulama(عُلَمَا) say that, doing that, can destroy your deeds;

158
00:12:19,702 --> 00:12:22,427
can destroy them; it just destroy all what you have done.

159
00:12:22,834 --> 00:12:23,994
تحبط الاعمال

160
00:12:25,007 --> 00:12:26,184
And Musa(موسى) is telling his people;

161
00:12:26,204 --> 00:12:27,257
وَلَا تَرْتَدُّوا

162
00:12:27,451 --> 00:12:30,407
Do not turn your back in fighting.

163
00:12:30,591 --> 00:12:32,140
فَتَنقَلِبُوا خَاسِرِينَ۝

164
00:12:32,450 --> 00:12:34,702
Then you will be returned as losers.

165
00:12:34,727 --> 00:12:37,875
If you turn your back away; you will return as losers.

166
00:12:38,542 --> 00:12:45,941
Not only did Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) turn their back to their enemy; they refuse to fight, to start with.

167
00:12:47,301 --> 00:12:49,884
It wasn't the matter of turning your back in the battlefield.

168
00:12:50,504 --> 00:12:52,878
They said; We are not going to fight.

169
00:12:53,264 --> 00:12:54,618
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

170
00:12:54,764 --> 00:13:09,770
قَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنَّ فِيهَا قَوْمًا جَبَّارِينَ وَإِنَّا لَن نَّدْخُلَهَا حَتَّىٰ يَخْرُجُواْ مِنْهَا

171
00:13:10,410 --> 00:13:25,230
وَإِنَّا لَن نَّدْخُلَهَا حَتَّىٰ يَخْرُجُواْ مِنْهَا فَإِن يَخْرُجُواْ مِنْهَا فَإِنَّا دَٰخِلُونَ۝

172
00:13:25,570 --> 00:13:30,656
They said; Oh Musa(موسى)! In it are a people of great strength.

173
00:13:30,923 --> 00:13:32,669
So what, if there are people of great strength.

174
00:13:32,703 --> 00:13:36,709
They said; And we shall never enter it till they leave it.

175
00:13:36,902 --> 00:13:38,382
When they leave, then we will enter.

176
00:13:39,069 --> 00:13:42,218
Look at this; they said that, the people in there are powerful and strong.

177
00:13:42,838 --> 00:13:44,431
They said; They're powerful and strong.

178
00:13:44,911 --> 00:13:48,217
So we're not gonna get in there until, these people leave.

179
00:13:48,563 --> 00:13:51,943
How do you think people who are powerful and strong are gonna vacate it for you?

180
00:13:53,757 --> 00:13:56,150
You already said that, they're powerful and strong.

181
00:13:56,516 --> 00:13:59,970
Do you accept, expect them to walk out and tell you come on in?

182
00:14:01,243 --> 00:14:03,709
You're already said that, these are people who are strong.

183
00:14:04,855 --> 00:14:10,881
But this is the negative passive stance of people who are humiliated.

184
00:14:11,101 --> 00:14:13,008
They want victory without paying the price.

185
00:14:13,455 --> 00:14:15,668
Let them leave and then we're gonna walk in.

186
00:14:16,275 --> 00:14:18,377
We want the victory; we want the Holy Land

187
00:14:18,484 --> 00:14:19,657
but we don't want to fight;

188
00:14:19,691 --> 00:14:20,841
we don't want to sacrifice;

189
00:14:20,957 --> 00:14:23,331
we don't want to pay any wealth;

190
00:14:23,386 --> 00:14:24,980
we don't want to give our souls;

191
00:14:25,173 --> 00:14:26,726
we don't want to put any effort;

192
00:14:26,873 --> 00:14:29,652
we want to go in there, in an effortless fashion.

193
00:14:30,712 --> 00:14:32,512
فَيَخْرُجُواْ مِنْهَا، إِنَّا دَٰخِلُونَ۝

194
00:14:32,532 --> 00:14:35,386
Let them leave, first and then we're gonna walk in.

195
00:14:36,412 --> 00:14:40,131
But there's still some good among them, so two men came ahead.

196
00:14:40,844 --> 00:14:57,230
قَالَ رَجُلَانِ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخَافُونَ أَنْعَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمَا ٱدْخُلُواْ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلْبَابَ فَإِذَا دَخَلْتُمُوهُ فَإِنَّكُمْ غَٰلِبُونَ ۚ

197
00:14:58,121 --> 00:15:04,342
Two men of those who feared Allah; on whom Allah had bestowed His grace, said;

198
00:15:04,505 --> 00:15:10,199
Assault them through the gate for when you are in; victory will be yours.

199
00:15:10,845 --> 00:15:17,441
They said; You attack them; open up the gate and that will be enough to defeat the enemy.

200
00:15:18,134 --> 00:15:19,693
Does this mean that it's a miracle?

201
00:15:19,853 --> 00:15:22,159
They just have to break in the gate and the enemy will leave?

202
00:15:22,426 --> 00:15:27,098
Or does it mean that if you break in the gate, the enemy will immediately lose, Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ).

203
00:15:27,378 --> 00:15:32,288
But these two men told them; enter the gate and if you enter the gate, you will win.

204
00:15:32,441 --> 00:15:34,008
That's all what you need to do.

205
00:15:34,068 --> 00:15:36,068
Just open up that gate and walk in.

206
00:15:36,748 --> 00:15:38,341
So these two men are willing to fight.

207
00:15:38,614 --> 00:15:40,467
They're willing to go in and fight.

208
00:15:40,793 --> 00:15:42,760
And they're encouraging their people to fight.

209
00:15:43,187 --> 00:15:46,222
What quality did Allahسُبحانه وتعالى describe these two men with?

210
00:15:46,528 --> 00:15:48,755
What quality do these two men have?

211
00:15:50,368 --> 00:15:50,928
Fear.

212
00:15:51,388 --> 00:15:52,492
يَخَافُونَ

213
00:15:53,089 --> 00:15:56,176
قَالَ رَجُلَانِ يَخَافُونَ

214
00:15:56,226 --> 00:15:57,342
They fear.

215
00:15:58,436 --> 00:16:05,194
This is very important thing to notice that you cannot fight the enemy unless, you fear Allahسُبحانه وتعالى more than you feel the enemy.

216
00:16:06,514 --> 00:16:07,774
You have to have Khash'ya(خَشْية) of Allah.

217
00:16:07,968 --> 00:16:12,913
You cannot face the enemy because as a human being; you have natural fear.

218
00:16:13,326 --> 00:16:14,806
You have natural fear from death.

219
00:16:15,246 --> 00:16:21,851
But if you have the fear of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, and you are afraid of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى more than you are afraid of the creation,

220
00:16:22,038 --> 00:16:23,745
then nothing can stand in front of you.

221
00:16:24,511 --> 00:16:30,093
And that's why the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; nothing can stand in front of them; nothing.

222
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:33,823
Because nothing can put fear in their hearts.

223
00:16:34,169 --> 00:16:35,783
They have no fear of the creation.

224
00:16:36,283 --> 00:16:41,209
The creation can present a bigger army; they can present stronger weapons

225
00:16:41,502 --> 00:16:45,495
but they can never put in their hearts fear more than the fear of Allah.

226
00:16:45,882 --> 00:16:46,661
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

227
00:16:46,681 --> 00:16:49,607
أَتَخْشَوْنَهُمْ ۚ فَٱللَّهُ أَحَقُّ أَن تَخْشَوْهُ

228
00:16:49,873 --> 00:16:51,047
Do you fear them?

229
00:16:51,181 --> 00:16:52,481
You need to fear Allah.

230
00:16:52,501 --> 00:16:55,226
Allah is the one whom should be feared.

231
00:16:55,493 --> 00:16:57,080
We should not fear the creation

232
00:16:57,390 --> 00:17:03,425
and that's why the men of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى who have the Khashyah(خَشْيَه); nothing can shake their hearts.

233
00:17:03,479 --> 00:17:08,271
Al-Izza-Ibn-e-Abdul-Salam(العزہ ابن عبدالسلام) when he walked and met with the leader of that At-Tatar(التتار);

234
00:17:08,885 --> 00:17:12,085
an emperor who was powerful mighty leader.

235
00:17:12,465 --> 00:17:16,827
Al-Izza-Ibn-e-Abdul-Salam(العزہ ابن عبدالسلام) walked in to meet with him and this man was famous with power.

236
00:17:17,413 --> 00:17:25,666
He was a blood thirsty leader from, Al-Maghul(اَلْمَغُوْل) who attacked the Muslim world and was destroying everything that he would see.

237
00:17:25,886 --> 00:17:28,148
In Baghdad(بغداد), they sacked it and they killed Two million.

238
00:17:29,322 --> 00:17:35,218
Al-Izza-Ibn-e-Abdul-Salam(العزہ ابن عبدالسلام) went with his students to meet with this leader of At-Tatar(التتار).

239
00:17:36,278 --> 00:17:37,864
 So, he started speaking to him.

240
00:17:38,124 --> 00:17:41,698
And then, he started raising his voice and pointing his finger in his face

241
00:17:41,878 --> 00:17:47,467
and threatening him with Hellfire and threatening him with the punishment of Allah and making Dua(دُعَا) against him.

242
00:17:48,787 --> 00:17:52,621
The students who came with Al-Izza-Ibn-e-Abdul-Salam(العزہ ابن عبدالسلام) started wrapping up their clothes.

243
00:17:52,674 --> 00:17:53,401
Why?

244
00:17:53,841 --> 00:17:58,162
They're waiting for the sword to cut his head and blood to splash all over the place.

245
00:17:58,509 --> 00:18:00,575
So they were wrapping up their clothes.

246
00:18:00,789 --> 00:18:02,793
So that, the blood will not splash on them.

247
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:07,500
When they walked out; they went to Al-Izza-Ibn-e-Abdul-Salam(العزہ ابن عبدالسلام) and said;

248
00:18:07,525 --> 00:18:08,460
What were you doing?

249
00:18:08,673 --> 00:18:11,010
How were you able to do that?

250
00:18:11,345 --> 00:18:19,768
He said; When I imagined the greatness of Allah in front of my eyes, then this man became smaller than a cat.

251
00:18:20,281 --> 00:18:26,654
When I imagined the greatness of Allah, this man; this mighty powerful military general became smaller than a cat.

252
00:18:26,794 --> 00:18:28,634
That is the Khashyah(خَشْيَه) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

253
00:18:28,968 --> 00:18:33,776
So these two men said; Just break the door open, and they're gonna lose.

254
00:18:34,829 --> 00:18:38,699
And they said; And put your trust in Allah if you are believers, indeed.

255
00:18:38,839 --> 00:18:44,812
What was the responsibility of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) after they heard the order from Musa(موسى) and they heard the advice from these two men?

256
00:18:44,898 --> 00:18:45,548
They said;

257
00:18:45,598 --> 00:18:50,462
قَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنَّا لَن نَّدْخُلَهَآ أَبَدًا مَّا دَامُواْ فِيهَا ۖ

258
00:18:50,833 --> 00:18:53,957
Oh Musa(موسى)! We shall never enter it as long as they are there.

259
00:18:54,044 --> 00:18:55,364
We're not going to go in; period.

260
00:18:55,604 --> 00:18:56,497
Don't try.

261
00:18:56,977 --> 00:19:00,156
Neither will your order work; nor will their advice do any good.

262
00:19:00,329 --> 00:19:02,876
We're not gonna go in and then, look at what they said;

263
00:19:03,196 --> 00:19:07,697
فَٱذْهَبْ أَنتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقَٰتِلَآ إِنَّا هَٰهُنَا قَٰعِدُونَ۝

264
00:19:07,990 --> 00:19:11,950
Go and fight with your Lord, we are sitting right here.

265
00:19:12,850 --> 00:19:14,344
Qa'idoon(قَٰعِدُونَ) means; sitting down.

266
00:19:14,477 --> 00:19:19,358
Look at the passiveness; sitting down, that is the state of many of us.

267
00:19:19,711 --> 00:19:24,718
I want you throughout the period of the story of Musa(موسى) and Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)

268
00:19:24,751 --> 00:19:26,491
now we're finished with Musa(موسى) and Firaun(فرعون),

269
00:19:26,625 --> 00:19:29,321
we're done with Musa(موسى) and Firaun(فرعون), you're not gonna hear about Firaun(فرعون) anymore.

270
00:19:29,571 --> 00:19:31,311
Now, we're talking about Musa(موسى) and Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

271
00:19:31,377 --> 00:19:38,703
From now on, I want you to always think about our situation compared it, with the story of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

272
00:19:38,857 --> 00:19:44,147
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not mention upto us those stories in Qur'an for historical purposes.

273
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:46,687
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is mentioning for us those stories

274
00:19:46,914 --> 00:19:51,340
because we are gonna fall in the same traps, but we have the guidance that will save us out of it.

275
00:19:52,606 --> 00:19:54,400
That is why, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى  told us these stories.

276
00:19:54,453 --> 00:19:57,882
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); they fell in those traps and they couldn't get out.

277
00:19:58,322 --> 00:19:58,669
And they became;

278
00:19:58,694 --> 00:19:59,679
اَلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ

279
00:20:00,075 --> 00:20:02,767
But this Ummah(امة) will commit the same mistakes.

280
00:20:03,047 --> 00:20:08,258
But because of the blessing of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; a group of them will always be on the right path.

281
00:20:09,058 --> 00:20:12,524
So we want to learn about this for our own benefit.

282
00:20:12,791 --> 00:20:15,290
They said; We're gonna sit down; we're not gonna do anything.

283
00:20:15,824 --> 00:20:19,010
We're gonna sit down here and Falastine(فلسطين) is gonna be free.

284
00:20:20,577 --> 00:20:23,992
The problems of Muslims around the world are gonna be taking care of.

285
00:20:24,972 --> 00:20:31,931
As if we are saying; that the problems we are living through now, are caused by our fathers, and our children are gonna solve them.

286
00:20:32,564 --> 00:20:37,027
We don't want to do anything or waiting for the Mehdi(مهدى) to come.

287
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:38,980
This is a state of passiveness.

288
00:20:39,060 --> 00:20:40,694
Qa'idoon(قَٰعِدُونَ); mean sitting down.

289
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:41,840
They're not doing anything.

290
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:44,887
But they want Musa(موسى) to go and fight with his Lord.

291
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:48,857
He is your Lord, He has promised you, He's going to do you good, go with Him and fight.

292
00:20:49,657 --> 00:20:52,806
Compare this with the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

293
00:20:53,329 --> 00:20:54,089
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

294
00:20:54,114 --> 00:20:55,409
أشِيرُواعَلَيَّ أيُّها النَّاسُ

295
00:20:55,462 --> 00:20:58,912
Give me your opinion; shall we fight the enemy or not?

296
00:20:59,519 --> 00:21:02,265
Al-Maqdad-Ibn-Aswad(المقداد ابن اسود) stood up and said;

297
00:21:03,099 --> 00:21:07,913
We are not gonna say, like what the children of Israel(اسرائيل) have said;

298
00:21:08,207 --> 00:21:09,740
Go and fight with your Lord.

299
00:21:09,873 --> 00:21:14,879
But we are going to say; Go and fight with your Lord; we are going to fight with you.

300
00:21:15,419 --> 00:21:22,672
Musa(موسى) is one step away from Jerusalem; the promise of Allah, which he has been waiting for four years.

301
00:21:23,606 --> 00:21:26,692
Musa(موسى) is almost there; he got it.

302
00:21:27,191 --> 00:21:28,758
He was freed from Egypt.

303
00:21:29,431 --> 00:21:30,904
Firaun(فرعون) was destroyed.

304
00:21:31,464 --> 00:21:36,077
And now, they are on the Gates of Jerusalem, he can see it with his own eyes.

305
00:21:36,597 --> 00:21:39,183
He can see the promise of Allah right in front of him.

306
00:21:39,437 --> 00:21:41,949
And in that particular moment, Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) betrayed him.

307
00:21:42,769 --> 00:21:45,582
It was a grim moment for Syedina Musaعليه السلام .

308
00:21:45,796 --> 00:21:50,113
Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) after that; he raised his hand, so Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

309
00:21:50,280 --> 00:22:04,683
قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّى لَآ أَمْلِكُ إِلَّا نَفْسِى وَأَخِى ۖ فَٱفْرُقْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلْفَٰسِقِينَ۝

310
00:22:04,951 --> 00:22:06,038
He; Moses said;

311
00:22:06,084 --> 00:22:13,980
Oh my Lord! I have power only over myself and my brother, so separate us from the people who are rebellious.

312
00:22:14,536 --> 00:22:16,307
I have no control over these people.

313
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:18,993
I have control only on myself and my brother.

314
00:22:19,153 --> 00:22:20,520
All of these are not doing me anything.

315
00:22:20,813 --> 00:22:24,247
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; Please separate me from the people who are rebellious.

316
00:22:26,033 --> 00:22:31,013
Because he saw that this nation who he served, and he brought them and delivered them to safety,

317
00:22:31,079 --> 00:22:35,395
now and when they're one step away from Jerusalem; they betrayed him and they refuse to enter.

318
00:22:36,288 --> 00:22:41,615
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has punish Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) because of that, and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

319
00:22:41,953 --> 00:22:49,055
قَالَ فَإِنَّهَا مُحَرَّمَةٌ عَلَيْهِمْ ۛ أَرْبَعِينَ سَنَةً ۛ

320
00:22:49,815 --> 00:22:52,295
يَتِيهُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ ۚ

321
00:22:53,015 --> 00:22:59,970
Allah said; Therefore, the Holy Land is forbidden to them for 40 years.

322
00:23:00,917 --> 00:23:03,875
In distraction; they will wander through the land.

323
00:23:04,082 --> 00:23:05,948
فَلَا تَأْسَ عَلَى ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلْفَٰسِقِينَ۝

324
00:23:06,108 --> 00:23:09,918
So be not sorrowful over the people who are disobedient.

325
00:23:10,458 --> 00:23:16,540
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made them wander in the desert for 40 years

326
00:23:17,753 --> 00:23:21,967
because of this sin, of refusing to fight in the sake of Allah.

327
00:23:22,173 --> 00:23:24,951
So they were in a small area; Sinaa(سِيْنَا).

328
00:23:25,918 --> 00:23:31,037
And they're going around in circles trying to find the way out; in a very small area, Sinaa(سِيْنَا) not very big.

329
00:23:31,724 --> 00:23:35,890
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made them lose directions.

330
00:23:36,103 --> 00:23:39,016
So they're going in circles traveling in Sinaa(سِيْنَا) for 40 years.

331
00:23:40,296 --> 00:23:43,330
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wanted to meet Musa(موسى).

332
00:23:44,184 --> 00:23:48,813
And He gave an appointment with Musa(موسى) to meet him after 30 days.

333
00:23:49,839 --> 00:23:56,090
He said; After 30 days; we meet in the holy place next to At-Toor(الطور); next to the mountain.

334
00:23:56,564 --> 00:23:59,073
وَوَاعَدْنَا مُوسَىٰ ثَلَاثِينَ لَيْلَةً

335
00:23:59,259 --> 00:24:01,879
And we appointed for Musa(موسى) Thirty(30) nights.

336
00:24:02,213 --> 00:24:05,752
Musa(موسى) was in a hurry to meet with Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; so he went early.

337
00:24:06,625 --> 00:24:09,145
The Mufassireen(مفسرين) say that, what happened was that,

338
00:24:09,465 --> 00:24:15,147
Musa(موسى) was commanded to fast for 30 days because fasting is purification.

339
00:24:15,854 --> 00:24:21,012
So Musa(موسى) will go through a period of purification for 30 days, before he meets with Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

340
00:24:21,379 --> 00:24:26,402
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله); fasting is a purification, Tazkiya(تَزْكِيَهْ); it is a purification for us.

341
00:24:26,629 --> 00:24:30,756
So, Musa(موسى) went through that period of purification for 30 days.

342
00:24:31,781 --> 00:24:34,887
Because of the smell and this is something that, some of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) say;

343
00:24:34,927 --> 00:24:38,380
because of the smell of his mouth, which is natural due to the hunger;

344
00:24:38,626 --> 00:24:43,715
Musa(موسى) used Miswaak(مسواك) to change that smell, and he went to meet with the Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

345
00:24:43,735 --> 00:24:45,142
Allah told him; Oh Musa(موسى)!

346
00:24:45,355 --> 00:24:51,561
Don't you know that, I love the smell of the mouth of the person who's fasting more than I love the smell of Musk.

347
00:24:52,554 --> 00:24:54,171
Go and fast another 10 days.

348
00:24:54,441 --> 00:24:55,821
He said; That's the reason, why?

349
00:24:56,274 --> 00:24:57,420
أَتْمَمْنَاهَا بِعَشْرٍ

350
00:24:57,947 --> 00:25:01,257
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; And we added 10 days to it.

351
00:25:01,913 --> 00:25:03,633
So the total was 40 days.

352
00:25:03,833 --> 00:25:08,665
During that period; during those 40 days; Musa(موسى) was fasting.

353
00:25:08,825 --> 00:25:12,705
وَأَتْمَمْنَاهَا بِعَشْرٍ فَتَمَّ مِيقَاتُ رَبِّهِ أَرْبَعِينَ لَيْلَةً ۚ

354
00:25:13,051 --> 00:25:17,867
And we appointed for Musa(موسى) 30 nights and add it to the period 10 more,

355
00:25:18,307 --> 00:25:22,553
and he completed the term appointed by his Lord of 40 nights.

356
00:25:23,272 --> 00:25:24,579
Musa(موسى) told his brother;

357
00:25:24,599 --> 00:25:30,541
وَقَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِأَخِيهِ هَارُونَ اخْلُفْنِي فِي قَوْمِي وَأَصْلِحْ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ سَبِيلَ الْمُفْسِدِينَ۝

358
00:25:31,168 --> 00:25:32,151
Musa(موسى) told his brother;

359
00:25:32,171 --> 00:25:39,680
Replace me among my people act in the right way, and follow not the way of the mischief makers.

360
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:41,520
So the leader of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) left;

361
00:25:41,580 --> 00:25:44,980
he has to appoint somebody else to lead them and the best was the Nabi(نَبِي); Haroon(هارون).

362
00:25:45,433 --> 00:25:47,921
Then Musa(موسى) went to meet Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

363
00:25:47,941 --> 00:25:48,494
Allah says;

364
00:25:48,627 --> 00:25:51,087
وَلَمَّا جَآءَ مُوسَىٰ لِمِيقَٰتِنَا

365
00:25:51,401 --> 00:25:55,929
And when Musa(موسى) came at the time and place, appointed by us.

366
00:25:56,096 --> 00:25:57,856
وَكَلَّمَهُۥ رَبُّهُۥ

367
00:25:57,936 --> 00:25:59,196
And his Lord spoke to him.

368
00:25:59,309 --> 00:26:00,851
Musa(موسى) went to speak with Allah.

369
00:26:01,571 --> 00:26:04,798
So Musa(موسى) is Kaleem-Ullah(كَلِيْمُ الله); the one whom Allah spoke with.

370
00:26:04,911 --> 00:26:09,384
And Kaleem(كَلِيْم) means; Allah spoke with him many times; not once or twice; many times.

371
00:26:10,657 --> 00:26:15,233
Musa(موسى) now, reached to the level where, Allah is speaking with him.

372
00:26:16,140 --> 00:26:19,420
Musa(موسى) wanted to get one step higher.

373
00:26:20,066 --> 00:26:22,048
He wanted to see Allah. So he said;

374
00:26:22,674 --> 00:26:25,361
رَبِّ أَرِنِىٓ أَنظُرْ إِلَيْكَ ۚ

375
00:26:26,241 --> 00:26:30,933
Oh my Lord! Show me yourself; that I may look upon you.

376
00:26:31,246 --> 00:26:33,946
Did Musa(موسى) say this because, he is in doubt?

377
00:26:34,286 --> 00:26:34,853
No,

378
00:26:35,093 --> 00:26:45,388
He said it because, he wants to achieve that high status and to enjoy the pleasure of seeing Allahسُبحانه وتعالى which is the greatest pleasure.

379
00:26:46,266 --> 00:26:48,046
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى);

380
00:26:48,226 --> 00:26:48,939
لَن تَرَىٰ نِى

381
00:26:48,999 --> 00:26:51,532
You cannot see me; you cannot see me.

382
00:26:52,852 --> 00:27:00,151
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى); Look at the mountain, and I'm gonna reveal myself to the mountain.

383
00:27:01,604 --> 00:27:04,730
Allah was to show him; a proof that, he cannot see Allah.

384
00:27:04,950 --> 00:27:11,632
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is gonna show himself to the mountain and Musa(موسى) is staring at the mountain.

385
00:27:12,732 --> 00:27:15,494
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى revealed himself to the mountain.

386
00:27:15,514 --> 00:27:18,747
And Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) says; Allah only revealed part of himself.

387
00:27:19,574 --> 00:27:23,845
The mountain was destroyed and crushed down and turned into dust.

388
00:27:24,479 --> 00:27:28,721
The mountain could not stand the power of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

389
00:27:29,068 --> 00:27:33,558
So, the mountain was crushed and destroyed and vanished, completely.

390
00:27:34,151 --> 00:27:35,111
فَسَاخل جَبَل

391
00:27:35,151 --> 00:27:42,710
It just went down in the earth because of humbleness to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and broke into pieces of dirt, sand.

392
00:27:44,263 --> 00:27:48,866
 Musa(موسى); when he saw the mountain, what happened to him?

393
00:27:50,332 --> 00:27:51,692
فَخَرَّصَعِقًا

394
00:27:51,712 --> 00:27:55,192
Musa(موسى) fell down in the state of shock, unconscious.

395
00:27:56,652 --> 00:28:01,288
Musa(موسى) fell unconscious because of the shock by just Staring at the mountain,

396
00:28:01,308 --> 00:28:03,908
what would happen to him if he was staring at the Allah?

397
00:28:04,921 --> 00:28:08,206
This was the reaction of Musa(موسى) when he saw the mountain.

398
00:28:09,026 --> 00:28:11,992
What would have happened to him, if he had seen Allahسُبحانه وتعالى?

399
00:28:12,179 --> 00:28:13,391
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

400
00:28:13,658 --> 00:28:24,530
فَلَمَّا تَجَلَّىٰ رَبُّهُۥ لِلْجَبَلِ جَعَلَهُۥ دَكًّا وَخَرَّ مُوسَىٰ صَعِقًا ۚ

401
00:28:25,175 --> 00:28:32,882
 Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; You cannot see me but look upon the mountain; if it stands still in its place, then you shall see me.

402
00:28:33,322 --> 00:28:35,235
So when his Lord appeared to the mountain.

403
00:28:35,495 --> 00:28:40,868
He said; he made it collapse to dust and Musa(موسى) fell down; unconscious.

404
00:28:41,182 --> 00:28:42,122
Then Musa(موسى) said;

405
00:28:42,342 --> 00:28:55,040
فَلَمَّآ أَفَاقَ قَالَ سُبْحَٰنَكَ تُبْتُ إِلَيْكَ وَأَنَا۠ أَوَّلُ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

406
00:28:55,420 --> 00:28:56,226
Musa(موسى) said;

407
00:28:56,733 --> 00:29:01,952
Glory be to You, I turn to you in repentance and I am the first of the believers.

408
00:29:03,339 --> 00:29:05,505
Did anybody see Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)?

409
00:29:05,739 --> 00:29:06,372
No one;

410
00:29:06,832 --> 00:29:09,985
No one has seen Allahسُبحانه وتعالى with his eyes.

411
00:29:10,692 --> 00:29:18,150
But Muhammadﷺ has seen Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) but not with his eyes.

412
00:29:18,744 --> 00:29:20,117
He saw Him with his heart.

413
00:29:20,817 --> 00:29:23,469
What does it mean that, you see Allah with your heart?

414
00:29:23,715 --> 00:29:27,342
When you're dreaming, your eyes are closed but you can still see and hear.

415
00:29:27,995 --> 00:29:30,921
When you dream about things; you see things; you hear things.

416
00:29:31,367 --> 00:29:36,294
So some of the scholar say that, Rasool Allah ﷺ has been able to see Allah in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), with his heart but not with his eyes.

417
00:29:36,994 --> 00:29:38,906
In Akhirah(آخرة); can anybody see Allah?

418
00:29:39,013 --> 00:29:40,826
Who are the ones who will see Allahسُبحانه وتعالى?

419
00:29:41,133 --> 00:29:42,733
Al-Mominun(اَلْمومِنُون); the believers in Jannah(جنة).

420
00:29:43,373 --> 00:29:48,618
The ones who are in the lower levels of Jannah(جنة); they would see Allahسُبحانه وتعالى every Jummah(جُمعَه).

421
00:29:48,985 --> 00:29:54,672
In the time of Salat-ul-Jummah(صَلوةُ الْجُمعَه); the people of Jannah(جنة) will go to a certain meeting place;

422
00:29:55,079 --> 00:29:58,239
and their seats will be reserved ahead of time.

423
00:29:58,886 --> 00:30:01,974
That's in the Hadith(حديث), You can just go and pick a spot and sit.

424
00:30:02,201 --> 00:30:05,827
You have the leisure to do that in the Masjid(مسجد), you can come and pick a spot.

425
00:30:06,167 --> 00:30:11,630
But there in Jannah(جنة) you cannot, the seats are already reserved; and on what basis are they reserved?

426
00:30:12,730 --> 00:30:16,068
How close you are to the Khateeb(خطيب) on Jummah(جُمعَه); that's in the Hadith(حديث).

427
00:30:16,515 --> 00:30:21,772
The seats; the closer you were to the Imam(اِمَام) in Salat-ul-Jummah(صَلوةُ الْجُمعَه);

428
00:30:21,792 --> 00:30:26,445
the closer you are going to be to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى on those meetings on Jummah(جُمعَه).

429
00:30:27,092 --> 00:30:33,293
So here in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), you can come and pick that spot; the earlier you come; the better spot and the closest spot you'll get.

430
00:30:33,360 --> 00:30:38,834
So you have the freedom of choosing this place; when you are in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

431
00:30:38,854 --> 00:30:40,698
but in Akhirah(آخرة); that's it, it's reserved.

432
00:30:41,721 --> 00:30:47,763
And the ones who used to sit in the first Saff(صَف); they are the ones who will receive the first Saff(صَف); the first line in Jannah(جنة).

433
00:30:47,830 --> 00:30:49,705
That is for the lower ranks of Jannah(جنة).

434
00:30:49,871 --> 00:30:54,931
And then the people of Firdaus(فِردَوس); the higher levels; they would see Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, twice a day.

435
00:30:55,465 --> 00:30:58,547
That is for the people of the higher levels of Jannah(جنة).

436
00:30:59,567 --> 00:31:06,890
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; as we have mentioned earlier; has punished Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)

437
00:31:07,236 --> 00:31:13,882
because of their refusal to enter into the Holy Land with wandering in the wilderness for 40 years; Ateh(اطیع).

438
00:31:14,515 --> 00:31:15,788
It was a punishment from Allah.

439
00:31:16,308 --> 00:31:19,033
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is very merciful and forgiving.

440
00:31:19,893 --> 00:31:22,139
So even though, it was a punishment for them;

441
00:31:22,493 --> 00:31:25,847
they were asking Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and Allah was accepting their Dua(دُعَا).

442
00:31:26,214 --> 00:31:31,930
They wanted food; they wanted water; they wanted shade; and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى was providing for them.

443
00:31:32,956 --> 00:31:34,039
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

444
00:31:34,059 --> 00:31:40,494
وَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْغَمَامَ وَأَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوَىىٰ ۖ كُلُوا مِن طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ ۖ

445
00:31:41,961 --> 00:31:43,454
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

446
00:31:43,761 --> 00:31:51,305
And we shaded you with clouds and send down on you; Al-Mann(اَلْمَن) and As-Salwa(اَلسَّلوى).

447
00:31:51,978 --> 00:31:59,187
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided them with clouds that is the shade to protect them from the sun.

448
00:31:59,894 --> 00:32:03,691
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided them with food and drink.

449
00:32:04,031 --> 00:32:08,622
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided for them shade and provided for them; Al-Mann-Wa-Salwa(اَلمَن وَالسَّلوى).

450
00:32:09,182 --> 00:32:14,242
Al-Mann-Wa-Salwa(اَلمَن وَالسَّلوى); The Mufassireen(مفسرين) have tried to explain, what it is exactly but;

451
00:32:14,308 --> 00:32:19,527
it is a blessing from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to something special; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى sent for them.

452
00:32:21,174 --> 00:32:24,766
Some of them said that, Al-Mann(اَلْمَن) and As-Salwa(اَلسَّلوى);

453
00:32:24,786 --> 00:32:30,368
Al-Mann(اَلْمَن) is some kind of extracts that come out from trees and it tastes like; honey.

454
00:32:30,955 --> 00:32:34,682
And some of them have mentioned that, it is honey.

455
00:32:35,108 --> 00:32:38,357
As-Salwa(اَلسَّلوى); most of Mufassireen(مفسرين) say; it's a bird.

456
00:32:38,637 --> 00:32:41,837
Even though, Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) were going through a stage of punishment.

457
00:32:42,311 --> 00:32:44,485
Because, this was supposed to be a punishment for them; why?

458
00:32:44,759 --> 00:32:47,405
Because they refuse to enter into; Al-Ardul Muqaddasa(اَلاَرْض المُقدَّسَ).

459
00:32:48,052 --> 00:32:49,498
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

460
00:32:49,684 --> 00:32:50,724
يَتُوبُ عَلَى التَّائِبِين

461
00:32:50,744 --> 00:32:53,810
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى accept the repentance of the ones who repent.

462
00:32:54,244 --> 00:32:56,710
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gives the human beings many chances.

463
00:32:57,197 --> 00:33:05,666
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has sent to Firaun(فرعون); nine Ayaat(آيات); Tis'ie Ayaat(تِسْعِى آيات ); one Ayah(آية) after another; giving Firaun(فرعون) a chance

464
00:33:05,722 --> 00:33:11,441
 but in the end; when Firaun(فرعون) refuse to accept any of them, then the punishment of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى came.

465
00:33:11,681 --> 00:33:14,828
 And when the punishment of Allah comes down; nothing can release it.

466
00:33:16,148 --> 00:33:21,679
So, with Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided them with this food, Al-Mannu-Wa-Salwa(اَلمَن وَالسَّلوى) is the food.

467
00:33:21,852 --> 00:33:24,527
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided them with the shade.

468
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:26,374
What else do they need?

469
00:33:26,840 --> 00:33:27,934
They need water.

470
00:33:28,560 --> 00:33:33,186
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And remember when Musa(موسى) asked for water for his people,

471
00:33:33,206 --> 00:33:35,292
the people came and asked Musa(موسى); we want water.

472
00:33:35,312 --> 00:33:40,354
So Musa(موسى) made Istisqa(اِسْتَسْقَىٰ); he asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to give them water.

473
00:33:40,767 --> 00:33:42,217
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

474
00:33:42,314 --> 00:33:54,466
إِذِ ٱسْتَسْقَىٰ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِۦ فَقُلْنَا ٱضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ ٱلْحَجَرَ ۖ فَٱنفَجَرَتْ مِنْهُ ٱثْنَتَا عَشْرَةَ عَيْنًا ۖ

475
00:33:55,085 --> 00:34:00,250
قَدْ عَلِمَ كُلُّ أُنَاسٍۢ مَّشْرَبَهُمْ ۖ

476
00:34:00,676 --> 00:34:09,702
كُلُواْ وَٱشْرَبُواْ مِن رِّزْقِ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا تَعْثَوْاْ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ۝

477
00:34:09,962 --> 00:34:14,058
And Musa(موسى) asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, to provide the Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) with water.

478
00:34:14,311 --> 00:34:22,670
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى); Hit the stone with your stick; 12 springs of water are gonna gush forth.

479
00:34:23,310 --> 00:34:26,532
For every tribe of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); they have their own spring.

480
00:34:27,566 --> 00:34:32,343
So the stick that Musa(موسى) had remember a long time ago, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى);

481
00:34:32,383 --> 00:34:34,027
وَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِينِكَ يَا مُوسَى۝

482
00:34:34,197 --> 00:34:35,357
What's in your hand, Musa(موسى)?

483
00:34:35,450 --> 00:34:38,401
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى knows the stick more than Musa(موسى).

484
00:34:38,721 --> 00:34:45,868
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has provided for Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); the food; Al-Mannu-Wa-Salwa(اَلمَن وَالسَّلوى) and the shade.

485
00:34:46,010 --> 00:34:47,727
وَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْغَمَامَ

486
00:34:47,904 --> 00:34:51,294
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى also provided for them; the water.

487
00:34:52,143 --> 00:34:59,386
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); they went to Musa(موسى), they asked Musa(موسى) to make Dua(دُعَا) for them.

488
00:34:59,929 --> 00:35:01,042
What did they want?

489
00:35:01,315 --> 00:35:02,602
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

490
00:35:02,622 --> 00:35:20,608
وَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَا مُوسَىٰ لَن نَّصْبِرَ عَلَىٰ طَعَامٍ وَاحِدٍ فَادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنَا مِمَّا تُنبِتُ الْأَرْضُ مِن بَقْلِهَا

491
00:35:21,254 --> 00:35:37,067
فَادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنَا مِمَّا تُنبِتُ الْأَرْضُ مِن بَقْلِهَا وَقِثَّائِهَا وَفُومِهَا وَعَدَسِهَا وَبَصَلِهَا ۖ

492
00:35:37,470 --> 00:35:39,348
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); they went to Musa(موسى)

493
00:35:39,368 --> 00:35:46,327
and remember, when you said; Oh Musa(موسى)! We cannot endure one kind of food.

494
00:35:46,974 --> 00:35:52,292
So invoke your Lord for us to bring forth for us of what the earth grows;

495
00:35:52,432 --> 00:35:59,696
it's herbs; it's cucumbers; it's Foom(فُوم), which is either wheat or garlic; it's lentils and it's onions.

496
00:36:00,850 --> 00:36:06,729
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided them with, Al-Mann-Wa-Salwa(اَلمَن وَالسَّلوى); special food from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

497
00:36:07,182 --> 00:36:14,111
They went to Musa(موسى) and they said; Oh Musa(موسى)! tell Allahسُبحانه وتعالى that, we cannot endure having one type of food.

498
00:36:14,131 --> 00:36:16,344
We want to have more variety in the menu.

499
00:36:17,251 --> 00:36:23,633
And they asked for; lentils, onions, garlic, and herbs.

500
00:36:24,380 --> 00:36:27,475
And other stuff that grows from the earth; vegetarians.

501
00:36:27,749 --> 00:36:31,587
All the stuff they want are some kinds of plants that come out from the earth.

502
00:36:33,267 --> 00:36:37,474
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is providing them with the best meat; special meat.

503
00:36:37,554 --> 00:36:43,174
